<title>USA: Times Mirror sets oddlot stock buyback.</title>
<headline>Times Mirror sets oddlot stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Times Mirror Co said Wednesday it had launched a voluntary &quot;oddlot&quot; buyback program for shareholders who, on August 30, 1996, owned less than 100 shares of its Series A and/or Series C Common Stock.</p>
<p>This program will permit eligible shareholders the opportunity to sell their shares back to the company. Currently, more than 5,000 shareholder accounts hold fewer than 100 shares.</p>
<p>Shares will be purchased by Times Mirror at the average of the closing market prices for Times Mirror Series A Common Stock from September 11, 1996 through October 10, 1996.</p>
